abstract: >
  The Meta-Globàlium is a hyperdimensional ontological model that organizes
  the totality of human reality along four reflective dialectical axes
  (subject/object, theory/practice, phenomenon/noumenon, plasma/world),
  projected from a 4D hypersphere onto 3D space, with a fifth radial axis
  of tempeternitat (time + eternity). It proposes a structural verifier
  for AI judgment in domains without ground truth, where the Good is
  defined geometrically as the property of not collapsing any dimension.
  The model consolidates a European philosophical lineage from Llull's
  Ars Magna to Xirinacs's spherical topology, and is intended as an
  open commons for adoption across AI research, philosophy, knowledge
  representation, and education.
